=E2=80=83

Hi Patrio Gabriel,

Provider outages and rate limits are the reason most LLM apps end up with a=
 queue, a retry layer, and an oncall rotation. They do not have to be.

OpenRouter accepts a list of models on every request. If your first choice =
fails or rate-limits, the request runs against the next one in the list aut=
omatically. Same response shape, same SDK, no changes to your app code.

Read the routing docs ( https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/provider-routin=
g?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&ut=
m_content=3Da1_feature_expansion&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+=
2026&utm_content=3DA2+Fallback+Routing&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=
=3Dcustomer.io )

=E2=80=83

client.chat.completions.create
( =C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6",
=C2=A0=C2=A0extra_body=3D{
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0"models": [
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6",
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0"openai/gpt-5.4",
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview"
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0],
=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0"route": "fallback"
=C2=A0=C2=A0},
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{"role": "user", "content": "..."}] )


=E2=80=83

A few things worth knowing:

=E2=80=A2 The list order is the priority order. OpenRouter walks it top to =
bottom.
=E2=80=A2 There is no extra fee for fallback routing. You pay the price of =
whichever model actually serves the request.
=E2=80=A2 Rate limits, 5xx errors, content refusals, and context-length err=
ors all count as failures. The next model picks up automatically.
=E2=80=A2 You can mix providers in the same chain. Anthropic, OpenAI, and G=
oogle together is fine.

The next email covers openrouter/auto, which picks the model for you based =
on the request shape. Useful when you do not want to maintain your own list=
=2E

