  <p style=3D"color: #000000; font-size: 16px; margin: 16px 0;" class=3D"ca=
49raw">Hi Patrio Gabriel,</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;"><strong>Provider outages and rate limits are=
 the reason most LLM apps end up with a queue, a retry layer, and an oncall=
 rotation.</strong> They do not have to be.</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;">OpenRouter accepts a list of models on every=
 request. If your first choice fails or rate-limits, the request runs again=
st the next one in the list automatically. Same response shape, same SDK, n=
o changes to your app code.</p>
 =20

