   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;">A few things worth knowing:</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;">=E2=80=A2 The list order is the priority ord=
er. OpenRouter walks it top to bottom.<br/>=E2=80=A2 There is no extra fee =
for fallback routing. You pay the price of whichever model actually serves =
the request.<br/>=E2=80=A2 Rate limits, 5xx errors, content refusals, and c=
ontext-length errors all count as failures. The next model picks up automat=
ically.<br/>=E2=80=A2 You can mix providers in the same chain. Anthropic, O=
penAI, and Google together is fine.</p>
 =20

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;">The next email covers <code style=3D"backgro=
und: #f4f4f5; color: #111827; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-fa=
mily: 'SF Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px;" c=
lass=3D"or-inline-code">openrouter/auto</code>, which picks the model for y=
ou based on the request shape. Useful when you do not want to maintain your=
 own list.</p>
 =20

